one of three values. "existing" when a current panel entry or review, on any panel, curates this disease with this MoI. "new_moi" when PanelApp Australia curates this disease for the gene, but not with this MoI (e.g., it lists only the monoallelic form and this association is biallelic). An entry's MoI can belong to another of the gene's diseases: "BOTH monoallelic and biallelic" on an entry that lists a dominant and a recessive disease does not give each of them both MoIs. Judge which MoI PanelApp Australia gives THIS disease from the entries and reviews that isolate it and from the disease names (e.g., "autosomal recessive" in an OMIM title). "new_disease" when PanelApp Australia does not curate this disease for the gene under any MoI (a disease it does not list, or a phenotype expansion).
